// Build settings that must never be committed with their real values — wired into the RunUp
// target through `configFiles` in project.yml, and surfaced to the app through Info.plist keys
// (see IOS_SETUP.md § "Coach backend").
//
// The real values live in `Secrets.xcconfig`, next to this file, which is gitignored. The
// optional include form (`#include?`) is what lets a fresh checkout still generate and build
// without it: the defaults below stay in place, and only the features backed by a secret fail —
// the coach endpoint answers 401 with an empty secret, which is the intended loud failure rather
// than a silent one.
//
// Order matters: the include comes last so a value defined in Secrets.xcconfig overrides the
// empty default above it.

// Shared app↔server secret for the coach proxy (`api/coach.js` checks it against its own
// RUNUP_APP_SECRET env var — the two must be identical). Not a per-user credential.
RUNUP_APP_SECRET =

#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"
